`expected_frechet` is the maximum distance any `P[i]` (candidate) is from `p0`. That's not the Fréchet distance — it's just the diameter of `P`. 

But you said the value `300` matches what was expected. So your expectation was based on `2·R = 500`... but the actual value `300` is `√90000 = 300`. So the expected Fréchet distance in the paper / context is `2·(5.5·GRID·√2)` for the corner `(6, 6)` = `2·300/something`...

