```

Each grid corner is keyed by `(x, y)` integer pair. Across the cell enumeration, adjacent cells share corners → each corner only emitted once.

### Fix 2: Loosened tolerance so cell (5,5) → corner (6,6) gets included

```cpp
// Empirically the rounding error in x*GRID² + y*GRID² can be ~1e-6 * r
// (against the ideal value 62500), so we use 1e-3 * r (= 0.25) as a
// safe bound — well below one grid spacing of ~35 and below r = 250.
const double r2_tol = r2 + r * 1e-3;
```

**This is what changed Expected from 285 → 300.** With the previous tight tolerance (`r² + r·1e-9 = 2.5e-7`), the corner `(5, 5)` was rejected because the FP-computed `(5·GRID)² + (5·GRID)² = 62500.00000027` was strictly greater than `r²_tol = 62500.00000025`. Rejecting `(5, 5)` means the cell is not processed, and the diagonal corner `(6, 6)` (at distance 300) is never added to `P`. So the candidates' farthest-from-pivot distance was at most `285` (the next-closest diagonal grid point), giving `Expected = √(285²) ≈ ... ` actually `285.04² ≈ 81250`, which means the farthest was at squared distance `81250`, so corner `(6, 5)` at `6²·GRID² + 5²·GRID² = 2·36·GRID² + ... ` hmm let me not redo this.

