// Compute the intersection of two convex polygons given as point vectors.
// Returns the intersection polygon (also a vector of points) or an empty
// vector if the intersection is empty (or has fewer than 3 vertices, in
// which case the simplifier cascade is fine with treating the candidate
// as dead — a degenerate intersection has no well-defined Fréchet
// representative).
