// compute segment-segment intersections — the clipping handles all geometry
// through half-plane tests and line-line intersection (only called when an
// edge crosses a half-plane boundary).  This keeps the constant factor low.
//
// Returns the intersection polygon in CCW order, or {} if empty.
//
// NOTE: Sutherland-Hodgman ONLY works when clipping a convex polygon against
// a convex clip polygon.  We always clip P (F-poly or a tangent-clipped
// polygon, both convex) against Q (Gi-poly, convex).  The result is always
// convex.
//
