Here's a breakdown of optimization opportunities, ranked by expected impact based on the timing data:

---

## 1. `Gi_poly` rebuilt |P| times per step — hoist out of inner loop (High impact)

`Gi` is computed once per stream point, but then re-wrapped in a `Polygon` object inside the inner `for (int i = 0; i < P.size(); i++)` loop:

```953:966:simplify.cppstd::vector<std::vector<Polygon_with_holes>> new_S(P.size());
        for (int i = 0; i < int(P.size()); i++) {
            if (dead[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            std::vector<Point> F;
            Polygon F_poly, Gi_poly, S_poly;
            {
                TIMER("find_F");
                F = find_F(P[i], S[i]);
            }
            {
                TIMER("polygon_construction");
                F_poly = Polygon(F.begin(), F.end());
                Gi_poly = Polygon(Gi.begin(), Gi.end());   // <-- same every i
                S_poly = Polygon(S[i].begin(), S[i].end());
            }
```

With |P|~35 (for e=0.5), `Gi_poly` is being constructed 35 times per stream point instead of once. Move it above the inner loop.

---

## 2. `S_poly` is constructed but never used in non-GUI mode (High impact)

`S_poly` is constructed every iteration but only used when `viewer && showS`:

```967:983:simplify.cpp
                S_poly = Polygon(S[i].begin(), S[i].end());
            }

            if (i == 0) {
                ...
                if (viewer) {
                    ...
                    if (showS) viewer->addPolygon(S_poly, c);
```

Gate the `S_poly` construction with `if (viewer && showS)`.

---

## 3. `intersect()` round-trips through `Polygon` unnecessarily (Medium-high impact)

The `copy_verts` timer (1.28ms, 20236 calls) exists because `intersect()` receives two `Polygon` objects, immediately copies their vertices back into `std::vector<Point>`, then runs the algorithm. But the data already started as `std::vector<Point>`:

```471:489:simplify.cpp
static void intersect(const Polygon& subject, const Polygon& clip,std::back_insert_iterator<std::vector<Polygon_with_holes>> result) {
    std::vector<Point> P_verts, Q_verts;
    {
        TIMER("copy_verts");
        P_verts.reserve(subject.size());
        Q_verts.reserve(clip.size());
        for (auto it = subject.vertices_begin(); it != subject.vertices_end(); ++it)
            P_verts.push_back(*it);
        for (auto it = clip.vertices_begin(); it != clip.vertices_end(); ++it)
            Q_verts.push_back(*it);
    }
    ...
    verts = orourke_cgal::convex_intersect(P_verts, Q_verts);
```

The full round-trip is:
- `find_F` → `vector<Point> F` → `Polygon F_poly` → `vector<Point> P_verts` (in intersect)
- `get_conv_from_grid` → `vector<Point> Gi` → `Polygon Gi_poly` → `vector<Point> Q_verts` (in intersect)

Adding an overload of `intersect` that takes `const std::vector<Point>&` directly eliminates the `copy_verts` step and the `Polygon` construction for F and Gi entirely (~1.28ms + part of `polygon_construction`'s 1.92ms).

---

## 4. Switch to `convex_intersect_fast` (Sutherland-Hodgman) for the inner loop (Worth benchmarking)

`convex_intersect` (O'Rourke, O(n+m)) is currently used, but `convex_intersect_fast` (S-H clipping, O(n×m)) is available and was noted to be faster for typical small polygon sizes (~12–19 vertices). `convex_intersect` accounts for 28ms of the 54ms `intersect` total. Worth A/B testing — just swap line489.

---

## 5. `new_S` vector-of-vectors reallocated every outer step (Low-medium)

```952:952:simplify.cpp
        std::vector<std::vector<Polygon_with_holes>> new_S(P.size());
```

This allocates and zero-initialises `|P|` vectors on every stream step. Hoisting `new_S` outside the `while` loop and clearing/resizing it each iteration avoids repeated allocation.

---

## 6. `point_in_convex` and `find_tangent_idx` both do one full O(|S|) pass over S

Inside `find_F`, `point_in_convex` is called first (early exit if p is inside S), then if p is outside, `find_tangent_idx` does another full pass. These two passes could be merged into one since both walk all edges of S.

---

## Summary

| # | Optimization | Approx. Savings |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Hoist `Gi_poly` outside inner loop | ~(|P|-1)/|P| × Gi polygon construction time |
| 2 | Guard `S_poly` behind `viewer && showS` | Saves ~1/3 of `polygon_construction` (1.92ms) |
| 3 | `intersect` takes `vector<Point>` directly | Saves `copy_verts` (1.28ms) + F/Gi Polygon construction |
| 4 | Try `convex_intersect_fast` | Potentially cut into the 28ms `convex_intersect` cost |
| 5 | Hoist `new_S` outside while loop | Minor allocation savings |
| 6 | Merge `point_in_convex` + `find_tangent_idx` | Minor predicate savings |

Items 1–3 are straightforward refactors with clear gains. Want me to implement them?

